section
-- Source module: Solutions.KFMTabM
/-!
# KFM 9b: fixed-point root tables by FM product recurrences — denotations and error bounds

All values are Gaussian numerators at scale `2^P` (`toC z / 2^P`); products are
`gmulT P z w = Q_P(z · w)` (the per-entry operation of `KFMPw.gmulP`).

* `geoL P c x n = [x, x c, x c², …]` (`n` entries, each step `Q_P(· c)`).
* `chirpL P c h g n`: `g_0 = g`, `g_{j+1} = Q_P(g_j h_j)`, `h_{j+1} = Q_P(h_j c)` (the quadratic
  phase `e^{-πi s j²/t}` with `h_0 ≈ e^{-πi s/t}`, `c ≈ e^{-2πi s/t}`).
* `prodF P n x = Q_P(⋯Q_P(1·x₀)⋯x_{n-1})`; `chirpEnt P s t j` is the `prodF` of the `d` axis
  factors `axTab P (s i) (t i)` at `j i` (`axTab` = `chirpL` from the `twiddle` roots `hRoot`,
  `cRoot`); `twTab P k j n = geoL` from `twiddle P k j` (twist table `≈ e^{2πi j m/k}`).

Error bounds (unit `u = 2^{-P}`):
* **`step_err`**: `‖Q_P(z w) - Z W‖ ≤ ‖z - Z‖ + 2‖w - W‖ + 2u` for `‖Z‖, ‖W‖ ≤ 1`, `‖z - Z‖ ≤ 1`.
* **`geoL_err`**: entry `k` of `geoL` is within `e₀ + k (2 e_c + 2u)` of `X C^k`.
* **`chirpL_err`**: entry `j` is within `4 j² u` of `G H … ` (`e(g₀) = 0`, `e(h₀), e(c) ≤ u`),
  provided `4 n² u ≤ 1`.
* **`chirp_axis_err`**: with `h₀`, `c` within `u` of `e^{-πi s/t}`, `e^{-2πi s/t}`, entry `j` of
  `chirpL` is within `4 t² u` of `gch s t j` (`RC.gch`, the chirp factor of `RC.chirp`).
* **`prodF_err`**: a product of `n` factors within `e` of unit-disc values is within
  `n (2e + 2u)` of the exact product.
* **`axTab_err`** (`≤ 4t²u` vs `RC.gZ s t k`), **`chirpEnt_err`** (`≤ d(8T²+2)u` vs `RC.chirp`),
  **`twTab_err`** (`≤ 4nu`), **`gtr_err`** (final rounding to precision `p`: `+ 2·2^{-p}`).
-/

